I carry the new coat, the grey sweatshirt, and the yellow hat to the till.
I put the things on the counter.
The shop assistant greets me.
"Hello," he says.
He scans the dark green coat and the sweatshirt.
Then he also scans the small hat.
"That is one hundred and eighty Euro altogether," he says.
"Are you paying in cash or by card?"
"By card, please," I answer.
I pay with my card.
"Do you need the receipt?" the shop assistant asks.
"Yes, please," I say.
He gives me the receipt.
I take the receipt.
I have my large shopping bag with me.
I pack the grey sweatshirt into the shopping bag.
But I do not pack the thick coat and the hat.
I need the winter clothes immediately, because it is very cold.
I want to put the warm coat on right away.
